      "notes": "COVERED — Exclusion validated 2026-04-06. Contrition is the inner precondition for genuine repentance rather than a distinct inner-being state: without deep sorrow for wrong done, repentance is merely a change of strategy. H1792 (daka, to be crushed/contrite) is distributed across repentance and grief registries. No lexical separation between contrition and brokenness exists in the Hebrew text — the crushed spirit (Ps 51:17) is simultaneously contrite and broken. The inner-being reality is fully addressed within its covering registries. Covered by repentance (#135), brokenness (#18), grief (#71). No further action required. Source: Session-A-v9-Empty-Words-Analysis-20260318.\n[AUDIT 2026-04-13] result=PASS  terms=22  verses=752  run_id=RUN-20260413_045206-AUDIT_WORD",
